From f39d3c63028439618594612cbfd0a24976254cee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fenleon <fenleon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:34:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] voip: peer orientation survives media-engine rebuild
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A peer camera off→on rebuilds the media engine, and the rebuilt one
seeded peer orientation 0 — the incoming video flashed CW-90. The
registry now owns a per-call peer-orientation cell: the live engine
writes every <video device_orientation> through
(CallEngine::set_peer_video_orientation) and every engine seeds from
the cell at attach (attach_engine), so a same-generation rebuild
inherits the peer's last-known rotation. The signaling handler also
records the value next to the SetOrientation forward, covering the
no-engine-attached window.
---
 src/handlers/call.rs        |  8 +++++
 src/voip/facade.rs          |  9 +++++
 wacore/src/voip/engine.rs   | 66 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 wacore/src/voip/registry.rs | 69 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 150 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

